WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
[Growing up,] there were things like water fountains.

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.460
Like “Black only.”

3
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.480
“Colored only.”

4
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.000
Or “White only.”

5
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:21.040
One of the things that was very evident was that public businesses were segregated.

6
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:35.960
There were businesses like Dairy Queen—sold ice cream and things like hot dogs and hamburgers, whatever.

7
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.760
This was before Burger King and McDonald’s.

8
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.260
Well, we couldn’t go up to the front window to purchase anything.

9
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.120
We had to go around to the back to purchase what we needed to purchase.

10
00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.280
And even going to the doctor.

11
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:57.520
If you went to a white doctor’s office, there was a white waiting room and a colored waiting room.

12
00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:04.540
And the colored waiting room was usually around the back of the building.

13
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:14.830
You got the same . . . Paid the same price, same treatment, but you had to sit in a different place from the whites.
